DTSTAMP:20260611T043850Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52699632285318
DTSTART:20260514T130000Z
DTEND:20260514T143000Z
DESCRIPTION:How much of your week is spent on work you probably shouldn’t
  be doing? Emails\, copy-pasting\, recapping meetings\, rewriting the same
  updates—these tasks quietly consume valuable time that could be spent o
 n higher-impact work.\n\n \n\nJoin Innovate Carolina at 79 Degrees West fo
 r a hands-on\, high-impact workshop designed for entrepreneurs and working
  professionals ready to reclaim their time. In this interactive session\, 
 you’ll learn how to build your own “AI executive team” using practic
 al\, accessible tools that can take repetitive tasks off your plate and st
 reamline your workflow.
GEO:35.757368;-79.164614
LOCATION:79 Degrees West
SUMMARY:Build Your AI Executive Team. Free Up Hours for What Matters.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/build-your-ai-executive-team-f
 ree-up-hours-for-what-matters
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043850Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52743889770050
DTSTART:20260514T160000Z
DTEND:20260514T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Who’s afraid of a big\, bad budget? If the answer is “me!
 ” you’re not alone. Budgeting can be an intimidating learning curve\, 
 but it is a useful skill. Telling the story of your project\, advocating f
 or what you need to make it flourish\, and navigating the financial system
 s of your institution are necessary skills when developing a successful bu
 dget. In this workshop\, we’ll break down the building blocks of budgets
  and bring you a new level of confidence for your next grant or fellowship
  submission.\n\n \n\n \n\nJoin members of the Arts and Humanities Grant St
 udio and College of Arts & Sciences Research Support Team to discuss:\n\n 
 \n\nCommon itemized expenses for arts and humanities projectsHow to identi
 fy if a funding solicitation is a good fit for your research needs and ant
 icipated expensesWhat resources are available at UNC-Chapel Hill for grant
  applicantsDefinitions for frequently used terms like F&A\, Fringe\, Allow
 able Expenses\, and Cost-ShareHow to format a budget\, in collaboration wi
 th your Contracts & Grants CoordinatorWhere to get started on creating a b
 udget for your projectCommon mistakes when designing a budget and how to a
 void them \n\n \n\nAll are welcome. Lunch will be provided. Please registe
 r by Wednesday\, May 6th to ensure your spot at the event.
GEO:35.913407;-79.052875
LOCATION:Hyde Hall\, Incubator Room
SUMMARY:Grant Perspectives: Big\, Bad Budgets
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/grant-perspectives-big-bad-bud
 gets
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
