 with Peabody Award-winning journalist and photographer\, Brian Palmer\n\nR
 SVP\n\nBrian palmer is a Peabody award–winning journalist based in Richm
 ond\, Virginia. During his 30-year career he has photographed conflict\, p
 olitics\, activism\, daily life\, and more around the world. His strength 
 is capturing life candidly\, clearly\, and creatively.\n\nPalmer strives t
 o tell stories in pictures about people and situations that might not othe
 rwise be told\, with integrity\, professionalism\, independence\, passion\
 , and compassion. \n\nPalmer’s photos have appeared in the New York Time
 s\, BuzzFeed\, Narrative.ly\; his writing in Smithsonian Magazine\, the Ne
 w York Times\, and the Nation\; and Audio on Reveal.\n\nPalmer’s documen
 tary\, full disclosure\, which appeared in 2011 on the documentary channel
 \, along with several magazine articles and photo exhibitions\, grew out o
 f three media embeds in Iraq with US marines. In 2019\, along with his col
 laborator\, Seth Wessler\, palmer received a Peabody Award for the Reveal 
 radio story “Monumental Lies.” \n\nBefore going freelance in 2002\, Pa
 lmer was a CNN correspondent. Prior to that\, he was Beijing Bureau Chief 
 for US News & World Report\, during which time he photographed for many of
  his articles.\n\nPalmer collaborated with his wife\, Erin Hollaway Palmer
 \, on the documentary make the ground talk WHICH evokes life in a historic
  black community that was uprooted during World War II to build a naval ba
 se\, now a top-secret US military installation. Palmer’s on-going projec
 t\, photography of Virginia’s neglected African American cemeteries\, gr
 ew out of the documentary.\n\nThe exhibit runs iuntil May 20\, 2026.
GEO:35.907875;-79.050132
LOCATION:Sonja H Stone Center \, Brown Gallery & Museum \, 
SUMMARY:Gallery Exhibit Opening: "Making the Ground Talk and Other Stories"
  by Brian Palmer
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/gallery-exhibit-opening-making
 -the-ground-talk-and-other-stories-by-peabody-award-winning-photographer-a
 nd-journalist-brian-palmer
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
CATEGORIES:Lectures
