UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52461695361889
DTSTART:20260603T130000Z
DTEND:20260603T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:A virtual onboarding series for principal investigators (PIs)\,
  faculty\, and project/program leads across campus. The program offers an 
 introductory overview of key responsibilities involved in leading and mana
 ging a research program. Topics will include developing proposal ideas\, s
 ubmitting proposals\, managing awards through closeout\, and navigating et
 hics\, compliance\, and research security.\n\n \n\nWhile the sessions are 
 especially valuable for new researchers\, all members of the UNC-CH resear
 ch community interested in strengthening their understanding of the resear
 ch enterprise and their roles within it are encouraged to attend.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:TeamOn: Research Team Onboarding
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/teamon-research-team-onboardin
 g
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043850Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51375565550491
DTSTART:20260603T160000Z
DTEND:20260603T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Certain individuals appear to succeed against all odds. Despite
  severe hardships such as living through war\, witnessing the death of a l
 oved one\, having a chronic illness\, being a victim of abuse or dealing w
 ith unemployment\, certain people not only adapt but actually thrive. Thes
 e people possess a quality known as “resilience.” This workshop will e
 xamine the characteristics of resilience and discover ways to introduce gr
 eater resilience into our lives.\n\n \n\nWorkshop Objectives\nAt the end o
 f this workshop\, you will be able to:\nDescribe what resilience really is
 \n• Describe the concept of resilience as it relates to children and adu
 lts\n• Describe the characteristics of resilient people\n• Describe ho
 w emotional control\, self-awareness and strong relationships relate to re
 siliency\nIdentify your own resilient capacities\n• Identify you unique 
 resilient strengths and areas for development\n• Recognize which situati
 ons are most stressful\nDescribe resilience building strategies\n• Descr
 ibe techniques to enhance resilience through changing your perception\, ta
 king decisive action and engaging in appropriate self-care.\n\n \n\nClick 
 on Carolina Talent registration link and select the “Request” button t
 o automatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Resiliency: Bouncing Back After a Setback
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/resiliency-bouncing-back-after
 -a-setback
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
