BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043850Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52897176999378
DTSTART:20260604T180000Z
DTEND:20260604T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Recruiting and retaining research participants is challenging\,
  especially when study teams are already stretched thin. This session prov
 ides a basic introduction to AI and\, more importantly\, shows how AI can 
 save time by making study materials clearer and more engaging. Attendees w
 ill learn the benefits\, limits\, and UNC-specific considerations of using
  AI in recruitment and retention workflows.\n\n \n\nWe’ll share plain-la
 nguage strategies and examples using Microsoft Copilot to draft and refine
  participant-friendly materials\, simplify dense language\, and reduce the
  burden of starting from scratch. We’ll also include a materials design 
 component led by Sarah Sutter\, Research Communications & Design Specialis
 t at the NC TraCS Institute’s Recruitment & Retention program\, focused 
 on how teams can use AI thoughtfully when designing and polishing recruitm
 ent materials.\n\n \n\nPlease note: This session is for all levels\; no pr
 ior experience with AI is required.\n\n \n\nPresenters:\nAli Sora\, MS\nRe
 search Project Manager\, Recruitment & Retention Program\nNC TraCS Institu
 te\n\n \n\nSarah Sutter\, MPH\nResearch Project Manager\, Recruitment & Re
 tention Program\n\nNC TraCS Institute\n\n \n\nRegister
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI in Action: Practical Strategies for Recruitment and Retention
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-in-action-practical-strateg
 ies-for-recruitment-and-retention
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
