X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043850Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51375586889526
DTSTART:20260610T160000Z
DTEND:20260610T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:For a long time\, the scientific community believed we were bor
 n with a certain number of brain cells and neural pathways and that\, once
  damaged\, they could not be repaired. In reality\, our brains are much mo
 re flexible. Depending on our lifestyle\, we can weaken or destroy connect
 ions\, or create new\, stronger ones. Engaging regularly in certain behavi
 ors and activities\, like physical exercise\, addressing mental health iss
 ues\, meditation\, and learning a new language or musical instrument\, sup
 port new wiring and can make existing pathways stronger. Essentially\, we 
 can slow down or somewhat prevent cognitive decline by doing challenging m
 ental exercises to keep our brains fit for optimal power.\n\n \n\nWorkshop
  Objectives\nAt the end of this workshop\, you will be able to:\nIdentify 
 traits of a healthy brain:\n• The ability to learn new skills\n• Judgm
 ent and intuition\n• Memory and perception\nIdentify barriers to good br
 ain health:\n• Depression\n• Chronic stress\n• Unhealthy lifestyle\n
 Identify methods for optimal cognitive health:\n• Engaging in new skills
  and mentally challenging activities\n• Meditation\n• Physical exercis
 e\n• Brain training\n\n \n\nClick on Carolina Talent registration link a
 nd select the “Request” button to automatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Mental Fitness for Optimal Brain Power
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/mental-fitness-for-optimal-bra
 in-power-70
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
