DESCRIPTION:Your body responds to the way you think\, feel and act. This is
  often called the “mind/body connection.” When you are stressed\, anxi
 ous or upset\, your body tries to tell you that something isn’t right. F
 or example\, high blood pressure might develop after a particularly stress
 ful event\, such as the death of a loved one. People with good emotional h
 ealth are aware of their thoughts\, feelings and behaviors. They have lear
 ned healthy ways to cope with the stress and problems that are a normal pa
 rt of life. They feel good about themselves and have healthy relationships
 . Poor emotional health can weaken your body’s immune system\, making yo
 u more likely to get colds and other infections during emotionally difficu
 lt times. Also\, when you are feeling stressed\, anxious or upset\, you ma
 y not take care of your health as well as you should. You may not feel lik
 e exercising\, eating nutritious foods or taking medicine that your doctor
  prescribes. Abuse of alcohol\, tobacco or other drugs may also be a sign 
 of poor emotional health.\n\n \n\nWorkshop Objectives\nAt the end of this 
 workshop\, you will be able to:\nIdentify the relationship between mind an
 d body\n• Describe how the body influences emotional and mental function
 ing\n• Describe how our emotions\, beliefs and self talk impact our body
 \n• Identify symptoms of a possible mind/body disconnection\nIdentify wa
 ys to enhance the mind/body connection\n• Describe methods for achieving
  balance in life\n• Identify ways to express feelings appropriately\n•
  Describe the importance of taking care of your health\n• Describe ways 
 to enhance awareness\nIdentify your personal action plan for mind/body con
 nection\n• Recognize the importance of consulting with your physician\n
 • Describe which mind/body tools need to develop\n• List outside resou
 rces for further help\n\n \n\nClick on Carolina Talent registration link a
 nd select the “Request” button to automatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Connecting Mind and Body for Healthy Living
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/connecting-mind-and-body-for-h
 ealthy-living
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
