DTSTART:20260708T160000Z
DTEND:20260708T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Anxiety is a highly uncomfortable feeling\, a lingering presenc
 e that causes physical and mental tension\, fills the mind with endless 
 “what ifs\,” and is capable of spiralling into episodes of paralyzing 
 anxiety attacks. People with anxiety will typically focus on reducing or e
 liminating it as the main problem\, whereas the real problem may lie elsew
 here\, with psychological avoidance. Psychological avoidance is a quick fi
 x to anxiety. It offers immediate emotional relief\, but it’s fleeting a
 nd comes at a heavy cost. When we avoid certain situations\, decisions\, o
 r actions\, it can ultimately lead to even greater anxiety and additional 
 problems.\nFor this topic\, we’ll examine the role of anxiety\, our mist
 aken belief that we should always be “feeling good\,” and the psycholo
 gical effects of avoidance. We’ll explore specific cognitive-behavioral 
 strategies for managing avoidance and dealing with anxiety. This is a comp
 anion course to the topic\, “Managing Worry and Anxiety.”\n\nClick on 
 Carolina Talent registration link and select the “Request” button to a
 utomatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Psychological Avoidance & Its Impact on Your Mental Health
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/psychological-avoidance-its-im
 pact-on-your-mental-health
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043850Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52958661069171
DTSTART:20260708T170000Z
DTEND:20260708T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Want to do more with AI? Agents can help. AI agents are designe
 d to work toward specific goals and complete tasks with less step-by-step 
 direction from the user. While they can be powerful and efficient tools\, 
 giving them too much autonomy can also create problems. In this workshop\,
  you’ll learn what AI agents can do\, where their limits are\, and how t
 o create and use your own using the UNC Library’s PromptLab. No prior ex
 perience with agents is required\, though participants who are new to gene
 rative AI may find it helpful to review our brief training videos before t
 aking this workshop.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the University Li
 braries and will be led by librarians Michele Hayslett and Lorin Bruckner.
 \n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offered remotely via Zoom only. Registrant
 s will receive a Zoom link\; those on the waitlist will not receive a Zoom
  link unless they are bumped up to a registered spot.\n\n \n\nAll registra
 nts however\, will receive access to the meeting recording and resources.\
 n\n \n\nYou can register through the Library Calendar.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Agentic AI
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/agentic-ai
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
