DTSTART:20260917T123000Z
DTEND:20260917T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:The first of its kind at UNC\, the inaugural Women’s Health M
 ultidisciplinary Research Symposium is dedicated to fostering interdiscipl
 inary connections\, collaboration\, and knowledge sharing amongst trainees
  and faculty passionate about women’s health research. \n \nHosted by th
 e Women’s Health Multidisciplinary Consortium (WHMC) and the Department 
 of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine\, this symposium is also supported by
  the Center for Women’s Health Research\, the School of Medicine’s Dep
 artment of Obstetrics & Gynecology\, Gillings Department of Maternal and C
 hild Health\, and more!  \n \nThis year’s theme is "Collaborate\, Innova
 te\, & Unite: The Future of Women’s Health Research at UNC". This sympos
 ium will create a platform for early-career researchers and medical profes
 sionals from various disciplines to showcase their work\, engage in meanin
 gful discussions\, and establish professional networks that will advance t
 he field. This year's symposium will feature keynote talks from Samantha M
 eltzer-Brody\, MD\, MPH\, Executive Dean of UNC SOM\, and Crystal Schiller
 \, PhD\, Director of UNC Center for Women's Mood Disorders.\n\n \n\nRegist
 er to attend here: https://apps2.research.unc.edu/events/index.cfm?event=e
 vents.go&key=CDBA\n \n\nAbstract submissions from graduate level researche
 rs\, medical students\, post docs\, medical fellows\, and any other early 
 career professionals are OPEN NOW & DUE June 30th\; 300 max word count: 20
 26 WHMRS Abstract Submission Form
LOCATION:Molecular Biomedical Research Building
SUMMARY:UNC Women's Health Research Symposium
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/unc-womens-health-research-sym
 posium
CATEGORIES:Academic Calendar
CATEGORIES:Meetings and Conferences
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043851Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52639033355962
DTSTART:20260917T130000Z
DTEND:20260917T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:This one-day course will be offered via Zoom only. Attendance i
 s required as it will not be recorded.\n\nThis interactive\, hands-on work
 shop will introduce participants to a framework for considering the conseq
 uences of using generative AI in qualitative research designs and workflow
 s (Paulus\, 2023\; Paulus & Lester\, 2024). We will start by acknowledging
  inherent risks and ethical dilemmas posed by the development of large lan
 guage models and how generative AI is challenging the essence of what it m
 eans to do qualitative work (Paulus & Marone\, 2025\; Paulus\, Lester & Da
 vis\, 2025). We will learn how to distinguish between methodological strat
 egies and technological tactics\, i.e. why researchers must first know how
  they want to work with their data before choosing the best tools to do so
  (Woolf & Silver\, 2018). We will then discuss the current ‘state of pla
 y’ regarding the various genres of AI-assist technologies available to q
 ualitative researchers and how to select the most appropriate platform. We
  will then compare and contrast several AI-assist platforms for managing a
 nd analyzing qualitative data. Finally\, we will discuss best practices fo
 r how to report the use of AI in research studies (Lester & Paulus\, forth
 coming) and how to reflexively consider the consequences of doing so. Samp
 le interview data will be used for the practice exercises. Workshop time w
 ill alternative between short lectures and demonstrations\, small group di
 scussions\, practical hands-on activities\, and application of principles 
 learned to the participants’ own research studies and data.\n\nRegistrat
 ion and fee are required for Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Designing AI-Assisted Qualitative Research Workflows
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/designing-ai-assisted-qualitat
 ive-research-workflows
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
