UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52127398770587
DTSTART:20261020T170000Z
DTEND:20261020T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:AI in Research: Driving Innovation Forward\n\nDiscover how arti
 ficial intelligence can streamline workflows\, uncover hidden patterns\, a
 nd empower breakthroughs in your field. Learn practical applications of AI
  through Odum Institute AIR series that can revolutionize your research pr
 ocess.\n\nThis course offers an overview of how AI tools such as large lan
 guage models (LLMS) can enhance early stages of the survey process\, inclu
 ding item generation\, questionnaire evaluation\, and survey refinement. T
 his session will highlight practical ways LLMs such as ChatGPT and Microso
 ft Copilot can support researchers while also addressing common pitfalls. 
 Participants will learn best practices for questionnaire design focusing o
 n writing questions\, response option development\, and question ordering.
  Ideal for researchers seeking to incorporate AI thoughtfully and efficien
 tly during survey development work. The first half of the session will pro
 vide structured lecture content\, and the second half will offer time for 
 participants to ask questions and discuss the specific projects they are w
 orking on.\n\nNo registration fees required but you must register to secur
 e your spot and receive the Zoom link. You must have an active UNC ONYEN t
 o register for this course.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI in Research series – Using AI in Survey Research: Practices an
 d Pitfalls (online)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-in-research-series-using-ai
 -in-survey-research-practices-and-pitfalls-online
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260611T043851Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52682483376859
DTSTART:20261026T190000Z
DTEND:20261026T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course will cover topics beyond the scope of the Introduct
 ory to Qualtrics short course. We will take a deeper dive into Survey Flow
  features including embedded data\, customizing the End of Survey experien
 ce\, Screen Out Management\, and implementing randomization. We will explo
 re methods of importing embedded data into your survey\, sending informati
 on from one survey to another\, and setting embedded data in your survey t
 hrough conditions within your survey. An introduction to automations will 
 be illustrated through an example use case that sends respondents to a dra
 wing survey after completing their survey. Finally\, we will create custom
  reports to share with others in the ‘reports’ tab. Course material wi
 ll be incorporated into a shared Group in which all participants will be a
 dded\, offering hands-on practice with shared Libraries\, and Directories.
  Additional features to be discussed include piping\, authentication\, and
  version management.\n\nRegistration and fee are required for Zoom link ac
 cess.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Intermediate Qualtrics
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/intermediate-qualtrics-9622
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
